# define.wick-dense

## .what
wick-dense = terse ideal for technical prose (john wick: few words, each loaded). state current truth in fewest words, then stop
aliases (one sense): wicked-up, wicked, wick-up, wick-down. verb: "wick this up". adj: "all wicked up?"
voices the ste overlay (define.simplified-technical-english): telegraphic, active, short, one word per concept

## .the three tenets
- few words → rule.require.brevity (blocker)
- point first, no wind-up → rule.forbid.rambles (blocker)
- no time-ordered log; state what IS → rule.forbid.chronological-accretion (blocker)
plus nitpicks: rule.prefer.short-sentences (≤~20 words), rule.prefer.one-instruction-per-sentence, rule.avoid.passive-voice, rule.avoid.articles-copulas, rule.prefer.active-simple-tense, rule.prefer.wickup-touched-prose (wick-up prose you touch, in scope)

## .scope
comments, briefs, plans, docs, commit bodies, error strings. exempt: verbatim quotes, code blocks, human-chat tone

## .the test
read it aloud as wick. would he cut a word? cut it. wind-up? none. recount his path? no — he states what is

## .example
👎 `// this function, after we tried a few approaches, now basically handles the reshape of the record before we persist it`
👍 `// reshape record. persist record.`
